Unity shader optimization for mobile:

Instead of 8 separate colorblind shaders:

```
Shader "Custom/ColorblindUniversal" {
  Properties {
    _Mode ("Colorblind Mode", Range(0,7)) = 0
  }
  // Single shader, runtime switching
}
```

One shader, zero duplication, instant mode switching.

40 hours saved.

Stop hardcoding game data in MonoBehaviours.

ScriptableObjects = designer-friendly data:

```csharp
[CreateAssetMenu]
public class RealmData : ScriptableObject {
  public string realmName;
  public Color themeColor;
  public RitualType[] rituals;
}
```

Designers edit in Inspector.
Programmers never touched.

Separation of concerns.

Coroutines are old school. Use async/await:

```csharp
async Task LoadRitualAsync() {
  var data = await FetchFromFirebase();
  await Task.Delay(100); // instead of yield
  ApplyRitualData(data);
}
```

Cleaner code, better error handling, modern C#.

Coroutines still have uses, but async wins for network/file ops.

Game state pattern in Unity:

```csharp
public interface IGameState {
  void Enter();
  void Update();
  void Exit();
}

public class StateMachine {
  private IGameState current;
  public void ChangeState(IGameState next) {
    current?.Exit();
    current = next;
    current.Enter();
  }
}
```

Menu, Gameplay, Ritual, Results states.

Clean. Debuggable. Scalable.

Unity instantiate/destroy = GC hell.

Object pooling pattern:

```csharp
Queue<GameObject> pool = new();

public GameObject Get() {
  if (pool.Count > 0) return pool.Dequeue();
  return Instantiate(prefab);
}

public void Return(GameObject obj) {
  obj.SetActive(false);
  pool.Enqueue(obj);
}
```

Use for: particles, projectiles, UI elements.

Smooth FPS, zero stutter.

Unity async scene loading:

```csharp
async Task LoadSceneAsync(string name) {
  var op = SceneManager.LoadSceneAsync(name);
  op.allowSceneActivation = false;

  while (op.progress < 0.9f) {
    // Update progress bar
    await Task.Yield();
  }

  op.allowSceneActivation = true;
}
```

Smooth transitions, no freezing.

Asynchronous = professional feel.

Robust save system:

1. Write to temp file first
2. Validate JSON integrity
3. Atomic rename (temp → real)
4. Keep backup of previous save
5. Version your save format

```csharp
File.WriteAllText(tempPath, json);
if (ValidateSave(tempPath)) {
  File.Replace(tempPath, savePath, backupPath);
}
```

Never lose player progress.

Coroutines = functions that yield control.

```csharp
IEnumerator FadeOut() {
  while (alpha > 0) {
    alpha -= Time.deltaTime;
    yield return null; // wait 1 frame
  }
}
StartCoroutine(FadeOut());
```

Perfect for: animations, delays, async operations.

 Better than Update loops for time-based logic.

Use cases:

1. Shared game state (no singletons)
2. Event channels (decoupled messaging)
3. Runtime sets (dynamic collections)
4. Designer-friendly data

```csharp
[CreateAssetMenu]
public class GameEvent : ScriptableObject {
  List<UnityEvent> listeners;
  public void Raise() => listeners.ForEach(l => l.Invoke());
}
```

Architectural superpower.

```javascript
match /players/{userId} {
  allow read, write: if request.auth.uid == userId;
}

match /global/{document} {
  allow read: if true;
  allow write: if false; // read-only for clients
}
```

Default deny, explicit allow.

Never trust the client.

Security = intentional design.
